<i>TURN-A TURN, TURN-A TURN, TURN-A</i>

00:01:13.710 --> 00:01:14.090
<i>TURN</i>

00:01:14.090 --> 00:01:14.590
<i>TURN-A</i>

00:01:14.590 --> 00:01:15.590
<i>TURN-A TURN,</i>

00:01:15.590 --> 00:01:16.090
<i>TURN-A TURN, TURN</i>

00:01:16.090 --> 00:01:16.510
<i>TURN-A TURN, TURN-A</i>

00:01:16.510 --> 00:01:17.510
<i>TURN-A TURN, TURN-A TURN,</i>

00:01:17.510 --> 00:01:18.180
<i>TURN-A TURN, TURN-A TURN, TURN</i>

00:01:18.180 --> 00:01:20.680
<i>TURN-A TURN, TURN-A TURN, TURN-A</i>

00:01:22.770 --> 00:01:27.060
<b>An Older Person</b>

00:01:48.100 --> 00:01:50.040
When I see a view like this...

00:01:50.040 --> 00:01:52.950
I fear the hatred between our people can never be forgotten.

00:01:53.400 --> 00:01:58.010
If that's the case, mankind may find itself locked in never-ending conflicts.

00:01:58.010 --> 00:02:00.760
And yet our opposition is filled with conflicting opinions on the matter.

00:02:00.760 --> 00:02:04.220
- Same with us.
 - In order to make them see eye to eye...

00:02:04.220 --> 00:02:07.840
I wonder if it might take another Romeo and Juliet style tragedy?

00:02:08.700 --> 00:02:10.560
It's an old earth story.

00:02:10.560 --> 00:02:13.150
One that Miss Kihel spoke of to you?

00:02:13.150 --> 00:02:14.190
That's right.

00:02:14.440 --> 00:02:17.650
Can we still not get a hold of that girl?

00:02:17.650 --> 00:02:19.660
You can see the state of Nocis for yourself.

00:02:19.660 --> 00:02:21.450
The Mountain Cycle, as well.

00:02:21.450 --> 00:02:24.620
Please find her, Ambassador Miran.

00:02:24.620 --> 00:02:27.150
Yes ma'am. Whatever it takes.

00:02:44.820 --> 00:02:46.060
Mr. Sid.

00:02:46.060 --> 00:02:47.350
Good, you're awake.

00:02:47.350 --> 00:02:49.340
Wake up, the enemy is here.

00:02:49.910 --> 00:02:51.770
Come on.

00:02:51.770 --> 00:02:53.940
Uncle Sid, good morning.

00:02:53.940 --> 00:02:55.730
We're packing now to leave.

00:02:55.730 --> 00:02:58.570
We're on the run again?

00:03:03.490 --> 00:03:06.160
So those were the two units with Corin.

00:03:06.160 --> 00:03:07.450
Have they been destroyed?

00:03:07.450 --> 00:03:08.950
No, they can still be used.

00:03:09.160 --> 00:03:10.370
Where are the pilots?

00:03:10.370 --> 00:03:11.960
We can't seem to locate them.

00:03:11.960 --> 00:03:14.170
And what of Corin's unit? The one named the Eagel?

00:03:14.170 --> 00:03:16.460
We haven't seen it.

00:03:16.460 --> 00:03:18.880
Could he have fled, rather than being destroyed?

00:03:18.880 --> 00:03:21.470
That man wouldn't have any reason to flee.

00:03:21.470 --> 00:03:23.590
He can only kill people or be killed in return.

00:03:23.760 --> 00:03:26.260
I'll have the truck come help pull it out.

00:03:26.260 --> 00:03:27.560
You've done quite well!

00:03:27.560 --> 00:03:29.550
It took us all night...

00:03:31.410 --> 00:03:33.350
Hey, since the White Doll made it out...

00:03:33.350 --> 00:03:34.440
That'll be enough.

00:03:34.440 --> 00:03:36.980
We'll leave the drill with Loran and get away from there.

00:03:36.980 --> 00:03:40.740
Isn't that the enemy's weapon?

00:03:40.740 --> 00:03:42.740
That should be able to help us out.

00:03:42.740 --> 00:03:44.660
Allow the White Doll to handle it.

00:03:44.660 --> 00:03:46.070
Alright.

00:03:46.380 --> 00:03:48.040
Old man Sid!

00:03:48.040 --> 00:03:49.450
Where are you going?

00:03:49.450 --> 00:03:51.580
This tunnel leads us southward.

00:03:51.580 --> 00:03:55.160
I've found another place with soil textures similar to Mountain Cycle.

00:04:00.690 --> 00:04:02.630
We've located the Eagel's head section...

00:04:02.630 --> 00:04:05.540
...as well as a few other scattered segments.

00:04:06.320 --> 00:04:08.470
There are also some south-bound footprints.

00:04:09.700 --> 00:04:12.470
Then could this mean Corin was KIA?

00:04:15.120 --> 00:04:16.860
That's what I'd expect of him.

00:04:16.860 --> 00:04:18.150
WaD troops...

00:04:18.150 --> 00:04:20.140
...continue following the mobile suit's footprints.

00:04:52.700 --> 00:04:56.150
That little shred of beef you gave me was delicious, Milady Kihel.

00:04:56.150 --> 00:05:00.060
Yes, the Militia's rations are truly excellent.

00:05:00.790 --> 00:05:03.350
It's from the Militia?

00:05:05.710 --> 00:05:07.450
Loran, lower the hand.

00:05:07.450 --> 00:05:08.730
Okay.

00:05:11.890 --> 00:05:14.750
Again, it resembles Mount Cycle.

00:05:14.750 --> 00:05:17.040
If we follow this path, will it lead us out?

00:05:17.040 --> 00:05:19.540
Yes, be patient. Don't concern yourself with it.

00:05:26.320 --> 00:05:29.250
Use that drill and dig in that spot right there.

00:05:35.990 --> 00:05:39.150
Even weapons can be used as practical tools if you do it correctly...

00:05:39.150 --> 00:05:42.770
- Isn't that right, Miss?
- Truly.

00:05:49.090 --> 00:05:50.740
Have you found anything?

00:05:50.740 --> 00:05:52.830
It's empty behind this stone wall.

00:05:56.100 --> 00:05:59.040
Isn't that formation the same as the caves we just came from?

00:05:59.040 --> 00:06:00.630
No, not quite.

00:06:00.830 --> 00:06:04.670
The sand's showing us otherwise. There's something in there.

00:06:04.670 --> 00:06:06.370
Is that so?

00:06:06.690 --> 00:06:09.260
Hmm, where's Milady Kihel?

00:06:09.260 --> 00:06:11.260
Didn't she say she was interested in this landscape?

00:06:11.260 --> 00:06:14.050
Milady Kihel doesn't know much about the countryside.

00:06:14.700 --> 00:06:16.470
Oh dear...

00:06:21.790 --> 00:06:24.560
It looks like she's more curious than ever.

00:07:03.500 --> 00:07:05.360
Excuse me...

00:07:07.790 --> 00:07:09.150
How impudent!

00:07:09.150 --> 00:07:13.450
Uh? Wh-Who are you? What are you doing here?

00:07:14.510 --> 00:07:17.370
You are...

00:07:17.370 --> 00:07:18.660
You're!

00:07:18.660 --> 00:07:22.240
Huh? Can I... help you?

00:07:23.520 --> 00:07:25.870
You're...

00:07:27.020 --> 00:07:29.050
Will Game...

00:07:29.050 --> 00:07:30.630
Are you not!?

00:07:30.630 --> 00:07:32.540
And who are you?

00:07:34.110 --> 00:07:36.470
I'm Dianna Soriel...

00:07:36.470 --> 00:07:37.770
Dianna?

00:07:37.770 --> 00:07:39.270
Will...

00:07:39.270 --> 00:07:41.470
Dianna Soriel?

00:07:41.790 --> 00:07:44.050
Dianna Soriel, you say?

00:07:49.500 --> 00:07:51.560
Someone's here.

00:08:05.020 --> 00:08:06.840
Who are you now?

00:08:06.840 --> 00:08:09.550
What are you doing here?

00:08:09.550 --> 00:08:11.970
No, I'm here to find the lady.

00:08:11.970 --> 00:08:13.470
I don't know where she is...

00:08:13.470 --> 00:08:14.640
The lady?

00:08:14.640 --> 00:08:16.670
My master.

00:08:19.780 --> 00:08:23.140
Uh, and who might you be, Madame?

00:08:23.140 --> 00:08:25.760
Madame? Me?

00:08:28.580 --> 00:08:30.860
I am truly deeply sorry.

00:08:30.860 --> 00:08:34.110
My behavior was quite rude, and I apologize.

00:08:35.710 --> 00:08:37.740
No, please don't.

00:08:37.740 --> 00:08:43.250
I've heard that I very closely resemble that Will Game, but how did you know that?

00:08:43.250 --> 00:08:45.170
It is because...

00:08:45.170 --> 00:08:50.250
I've heard the legend of the man from the Game family who looked after a lady from the moon.

00:08:50.250 --> 00:08:54.130
I was told this tale as a little girl, and when I saw you, I thought you might be that same Will Game.

00:08:54.130 --> 00:08:55.630
Then, I'm sorry.

00:08:55.630 --> 00:08:57.640
I am simply a lone man digging in this place.

00:08:57.640 --> 00:08:59.300
Dianna Soriel!

00:09:01.390 --> 00:09:03.270
What the hell are you doing here!?

00:09:03.270 --> 00:09:05.770
You're wrong! That person is Lady Kihel!

00:09:05.770 --> 00:09:08.140
It's not her Majesty Dianna!

00:09:11.210 --> 00:09:13.440
Teteth, what is it?

00:09:18.800 --> 00:09:20.950
Then this is the wrong person?

00:09:20.950 --> 00:09:22.870
Just look at her outfit and you'll see!

00:09:22.870 --> 00:09:25.040
She is the eldest daughter of the Heim family of Vicinity,

00:09:25.040 --> 00:09:26.960
Lady Kihel!

00:09:26.960 --> 00:09:28.460
I'm very sorry.

00:09:28.460 --> 00:09:32.170
I had taken interest in your husband's activities here...

00:09:32.170 --> 00:09:34.050
My husband?

00:09:34.050 --> 00:09:39.970
Oh, I see. Dianna Counter's leader wouldn't have a reason to be in a place like this.

00:09:39.970 --> 00:09:42.550
I'm sorry I worried you.

00:09:45.780 --> 00:09:48.650
You're a good guy. You deeply care about your master.

00:09:48.650 --> 00:09:51.140
That's because the lady is very important to me.

00:09:52.710 --> 00:09:55.240
l am Loran Cehack.

00:09:55.240 --> 00:09:57.860
l was hired by the Heim family.

00:09:57.860 --> 00:09:59.450
That family who runs the mines?

00:09:59.450 --> 00:10:00.200
Yes.

00:10:00.450 --> 00:10:01.950
Oh, I understand.

00:10:01.950 --> 00:10:05.660
That must be why the lady is so interested in my work.

00:10:05.660 --> 00:10:07.460
Yes.

00:10:07.460 --> 00:10:09.540
This is Mr. Will Game.

00:10:09.540 --> 00:10:11.250
Mr. Will Game?

00:10:11.250 --> 00:10:12.880
Darling, it's time for lunch.

00:10:12.880 --> 00:10:16.170
Sorry about that. I've been nothing but trouble for you lately.

00:10:16.170 --> 00:10:17.840
What is he excavating?

00:10:17.840 --> 00:10:20.790
I haven't had a chance to ask him.

00:10:20.790 --> 00:10:23.850
Do they know the truth of what you're excavating yet?

00:10:23.850 --> 00:10:25.470
The truth?

00:10:30.000 --> 00:10:31.770
The Mustached Mobile Suit went in there.

00:10:31.770 --> 00:10:34.350
Is the Militia hiding around here?

00:10:36.500 --> 00:10:38.450
Still, it seems the craters down there...

00:10:38.450 --> 00:10:41.450
...are much different from the others we've seen off-world.

00:10:41.450 --> 00:10:43.530
That's because the earth is bigger than the moon.

00:10:43.530 --> 00:10:45.450
I'll report to Ensign Poe.

00:10:45.450 --> 00:10:47.660
She'll probably give herself all the credit, though.

00:10:47.660 --> 00:10:49.240
Can't be helped, I'm afraid.

00:10:55.520 --> 00:10:58.260
Thank you for splitting and sharing your lunch with us.

00:10:58.260 --> 00:10:59.840
I'm sorry for the inconvenience.

00:10:59.840 --> 00:11:02.640
There are plenty of sandwiches for everyone.

00:11:02.640 --> 00:11:03.550
Here.

00:11:03.550 --> 00:11:04.560
Yes, thank you.

00:11:04.560 --> 00:11:06.640
But having done all of this by himself...

00:11:06.640 --> 00:11:08.680
Your husband is really something else.

00:11:08.930 --> 00:11:12.060
I was shocked when I first saw it myself.

00:11:12.060 --> 00:11:17.230
He's been following the instructions he discovered in an old ancestor's diary, and he dug up all this.

00:11:17.230 --> 00:11:19.150
Is that a tunnel?

00:11:19.150 --> 00:11:20.200
I don't know.

00:11:20.450 --> 00:11:23.690
Madame, your sandwich was great.

00:11:23.690 --> 00:11:25.530
So, can this ship travel in outer space?

00:11:25.530 --> 00:11:26.950
That's what it looks like.

00:11:26.950 --> 00:11:29.960
It looks like a relic built in the same era as the White Doll.

00:11:29.960 --> 00:11:32.710
What made you decide to dig this thing up?

00:11:32.710 --> 00:11:35.670
My reason? Well, that's...

00:11:35.670 --> 00:11:39.460
You want to reach the Moon and find out about your ancestor's old love story, right?

00:11:39.460 --> 00:11:41.550
Don't say that, Ms. Teteth...

00:11:41.550 --> 00:11:46.640
We live in an era of change, so he claims he's doing this for the Militia's sake.

00:11:46.640 --> 00:11:51.560
But he really wants to meet the tale's other lover, Dianna Soriel. Isn't that funny?

00:11:51.560 --> 00:11:55.770
Well, if I look over Loran's White Doll, I may be able to confirm my initial suspicion...

00:11:55.770 --> 00:11:58.440
...that this ship can reach space.

00:11:58.440 --> 00:12:02.150
We know that the people working for Dianna Counter live on the moon...

00:12:02.150 --> 00:12:04.570
So the legend of Dianna is real.

00:12:04.570 --> 00:12:06.950
Will Game... He's not the same man from back then...

00:12:06.950 --> 00:12:09.370
...but his ancestor's blood is clearly in him.

00:12:09.370 --> 00:12:12.660
This place smells just like Kingsley did...

00:12:27.990 --> 00:12:30.140
Must you embark on this journey?

00:12:30.140 --> 00:12:33.690
You've made requests of several men.

00:12:33.690 --> 00:12:38.730
Then, I'll have no choice but to travel east and bring their treasured bird back to you.

00:12:38.730 --> 00:12:41.440
I will return.

00:12:41.440 --> 00:12:44.150
When that happens, I ask for your hand in marriage.

00:12:44.510 --> 00:12:47.570
Of course. Please return to me safely.

00:13:02.110 --> 00:13:03.260
So, this here?

00:13:03.260 --> 00:13:06.180
You mean this could be used to store Mobile Suits?

00:13:06.180 --> 00:13:11.970
Yes, that's right. There must be some way for us to get inside it, Mr. Will.

00:13:13.280 --> 00:13:16.430
Was this the one that they dug out of that mountain?

00:13:20.440 --> 00:13:22.730
Is that really true?

00:13:23.090 --> 00:13:26.080
It looks brand new.

00:13:26.080 --> 00:13:29.160
It's rude to mess with someone's mechanical doll like that.

00:13:29.160 --> 00:13:32.360
I'm sorry. I just touched it and it opened.

00:13:33.680 --> 00:13:35.960
This is the first time I've seen something like this.

00:13:35.960 --> 00:13:37.870
Naturally, I was only curious about it.

00:13:37.870 --> 00:13:39.960
That makes sense, but...

00:13:39.960 --> 00:13:43.550
Hey, how do you know how to operate this Mechanical Doll?

00:13:43.550 --> 00:13:45.800
Please tell me all about it!

00:13:46.610 --> 00:13:48.430
You're from the Moonrace, aren't you?

00:13:48.430 --> 00:13:49.260
How did-

00:13:49.260 --> 00:13:50.760
l can smell it.

00:13:50.760 --> 00:13:52.430
Laura's from the Moonrace, but...

00:13:52.430 --> 00:13:54.560
Loran is just a citizen of Vicinity.

00:13:54.560 --> 00:13:56.140
What do you mean?

00:13:56.140 --> 00:13:58.440
You know, there are some people on earth...

00:13:58.440 --> 00:14:00.850
...whose ancestry can be traced back to the moon.

00:14:01.290 --> 00:14:02.440
This way.

00:14:02.440 --> 00:14:04.350
That hurts.

00:14:05.380 --> 00:14:08.360
Uncovering a ruin like that is no easy job.

00:14:08.360 --> 00:14:09.240
It's a hot spring!

00:14:09.240 --> 00:14:10.650
That's right.

00:14:12.380 --> 00:14:14.740
You should join me.

00:14:16.180 --> 00:14:18.920
Are you taking advantage of a woman by letting her go in first?

00:14:18.920 --> 00:14:21.080
No, that's not it at all.

00:14:21.080 --> 00:14:28.090
Or, are you afraid you'll make that woman of yours sad by bathing in a hot spring with another woman?

00:14:28.090 --> 00:14:32.050
That's not what I was thinking!

00:14:36.200 --> 00:14:37.930
Are you good at swimming?

00:14:37.930 --> 00:14:39.440
No, not really.

00:14:39.440 --> 00:14:43.230
You've never tried it in a sizable body of water like this, right?

00:14:43.230 --> 00:14:44.940
Right.

00:14:44.940 --> 00:14:46.940
Take off your clothes and try just floating.

00:14:46.940 --> 00:14:48.030
It's feels great.

00:14:48.030 --> 00:14:48.820
Lay in the water?

00:14:49.030 --> 00:14:50.530
Face towards the sky.

00:14:50.530 --> 00:14:51.450
Like this?

00:14:51.450 --> 00:14:53.020
That's it.

00:14:53.800 --> 00:14:55.940
It's like being on the moon!

00:14:57.600 --> 00:15:00.960
If you are from the Moonrace, why are you helping the Militia solders?

00:15:00.960 --> 00:15:03.130
You're from the Moonrace as well.

00:15:03.130 --> 00:15:04.460
My ancestors were.

00:15:04.460 --> 00:15:07.090
After the space ship has been excavated, what are you planning to do?

00:15:07.340 --> 00:15:08.630
What am I planning?

00:15:08.630 --> 00:15:11.880
Doesn't it seem odd to you that those old fossilized items can even move?

00:15:11.880 --> 00:15:14.880
I'm getting out.

00:15:14.880 --> 00:15:18.130
Some guests have arrived. I guess it's time for me to go too.

00:15:21.790 --> 00:15:23.560
I need to borrow this pick-axe.

00:15:23.560 --> 00:15:25.060
Go ahead.

00:15:33.380 --> 00:15:35.330
l would like to ask you something.

00:15:35.330 --> 00:15:36.540
What's that?

00:15:36.540 --> 00:15:38.620
Mr. Will's ancestor, Sir Will.

00:15:38.620 --> 00:15:42.680
What happened to him after he went to the east?

00:15:42.680 --> 00:15:44.750
Although he did find his precious Bird of Happiness...

00:15:44.750 --> 00:15:46.380
He landed on the west coast...

00:15:46.380 --> 00:15:49.970
...and died in an airship accident on the journey back here.

00:15:49.970 --> 00:15:52.630
The old tale in the children's picture books was accurate.

00:15:52.630 --> 00:15:54.050
Did you believe them?

00:15:54.050 --> 00:15:55.550
Children's books...

00:15:55.550 --> 00:15:59.850
A few of the first generation Will's possessions were found in the ships remnants...

00:15:59.850 --> 00:16:04.260
But my own grandfather told me of this story himself.

00:16:02.290 --> 00:16:05.230
- Before Will could return...

00:16:05.230 --> 00:16:08.530
The moon had sent a ship to pick me up.

00:16:08.530 --> 00:16:10.530
That's why l never knew what really happened...

00:16:10.740 --> 00:16:14.150
Women tend like this sort of story.

00:16:15.590 --> 00:16:21.040
On the way back to the moon, All I did was read reports and sort ordeals on the moon that occurred while I was away.

00:16:21.040 --> 00:16:24.950
After I finished them, they put me back into cryo-stasis.

00:16:26.480 --> 00:16:28.040
Is that...

00:16:28.040 --> 00:16:30.460
The only thing there is for a Queen?

00:16:37.200 --> 00:16:39.260
Lady?

00:16:49.880 --> 00:16:52.210
Milady Kihel!

00:16:52.210 --> 00:16:54.700
So he really does worry about about his Master's opinion...

00:16:59.660 --> 00:17:00.950
It's a WaD!

00:17:00.950 --> 00:17:02.910
Milady, the enemy has come here!

00:17:03.390 --> 00:17:05.750
Teteth, the lady is counting on you.

00:17:05.750 --> 00:17:07.750
- Is it Dianna Counter?
- Right

00:17:07.750 --> 00:17:09.740
The soldiers found out...

00:17:10.900 --> 00:17:13.050
Will, please hide yourself in here!

00:17:13.050 --> 00:17:15.430
Did Dianna Counter find us?

00:17:15.430 --> 00:17:18.180
I'll lead them to the cave where we came from earlier.

00:17:31.290 --> 00:17:32.730
Is it around here?

00:17:32.730 --> 00:17:33.940
This is where we saw it.

00:17:33.940 --> 00:17:35.530
Come out here, Laura!

00:17:35.530 --> 00:17:37.060
In that valley!

00:17:37.510 --> 00:17:38.940
In there?

00:17:48.480 --> 00:17:49.960
l found it!

00:17:49.960 --> 00:17:52.250
WaD troops... go after the Mustached Mobile Suit!

00:17:52.250 --> 00:17:54.130
I'm going to catch that Laura...

00:17:54.130 --> 00:17:55.960
...and snap her precious little neck!

00:18:03.430 --> 00:18:05.840
If you want to be so persistent, then watch this!

00:18:09.290 --> 00:18:11.900
If I can just immobilize them, that'll make them give in.

00:18:27.100 --> 00:18:29.330
Commander Phil and his men are still...

00:18:29.330 --> 00:18:33.170
It seems bringing the soldiers to earth has only aggravated their aggression.

00:18:33.170 --> 00:18:35.100
Are you all right?

00:18:35.100 --> 00:18:36.720
Yes, I'm fine.

00:18:36.970 --> 00:18:40.050
The moon's troops are terrifying, aren't they?

00:18:40.050 --> 00:18:42.640
Yes, they send a chill right down my spine.

00:18:42.640 --> 00:18:44.430
I agree completely.

00:18:44.430 --> 00:18:46.550
Who is this person?

00:18:47.580 --> 00:18:49.930
What happened to the WaD troops?

00:18:50.290 --> 00:18:52.790
If they've been buried, they can dig themselves out.

00:18:52.790 --> 00:18:54.940
Where is that Mustached mobile suit?

00:18:54.940 --> 00:18:57.060
Has she gone back underground?

00:18:59.300 --> 00:19:00.940
There it is!

00:19:01.300 --> 00:19:03.240
If there aren't any WaD Troops left, get out of the way!

00:19:03.240 --> 00:19:04.940
I can't attack it now!

00:19:10.750 --> 00:19:12.460
This is unbelievable.

00:19:12.460 --> 00:19:14.460
Could I try using this so-called I-Field?

00:19:27.700 --> 00:19:29.810
Go to hell!

00:19:37.580 --> 00:19:39.230
The Mustache's...?

00:19:40.590 --> 00:19:42.650
Using my arm?

00:19:55.890 --> 00:19:58.540
Ejecting the head... That damned Mustache!

00:20:07.490 --> 00:20:09.850
I'm a pathetic woman!

00:20:09.850 --> 00:20:13.440
Phil treats me like a Lieutenant...

00:20:13.440 --> 00:20:16.820
...and yet I can't even outperform some worthless no-rank pilot!

00:20:27.010 --> 00:20:29.330
You can stay here, but I won't have much to show in return.

00:20:29.330 --> 00:20:32.740
What do you mean? I'd love to inspect your ancestor's old diary.

00:20:33.600 --> 00:20:35.460
Don't you want to come?

00:20:35.460 --> 00:20:36.960
Please go on ahead.

00:20:36.960 --> 00:20:38.450
Sure.

00:20:39.190 --> 00:20:42.260
This is indeed Will Game's old house at Albany...

00:20:42.260 --> 00:20:44.550
Even the old watermill's still here...

00:20:46.490 --> 00:20:48.430
But the wheel's missing.

00:20:48.430 --> 00:20:50.560
Could this be the tree planted by the first Will Game?

00:20:52.410 --> 00:20:55.050
Even his trees have grown quite large.

00:20:57.290 --> 00:20:59.440
That's right...

00:20:59.440 --> 00:21:01.930
That's the room l stayed in all those years ago...

00:21:03.000 --> 00:21:05.570
This part of the mansion hasn't changed at all.

00:21:05.570 --> 00:21:08.450
Miss Kihel, why don't you come in and wash up?

00:21:09.090 --> 00:21:11.650
Yes, thank you.

00:21:13.890 --> 00:21:16.120
Where are you, Mr. Will?

00:21:16.120 --> 00:21:17.830
Hold on a moment.

00:21:21.400 --> 00:21:22.840
Hey, miss...

00:21:22.840 --> 00:21:24.920
Since you've taken such great interest in the story of Dianna and Will,

00:21:24.920 --> 00:21:27.460
Allow me show you something interesting.

00:21:39.000 --> 00:21:42.440
I don't know whether it's a myth or not, but can you see this feather?

00:21:42.440 --> 00:21:47.700
This is the same one from the bird of happiness that Will had been searching for.

00:21:47.700 --> 00:21:51.230
I found it in the possessions recovered from the downed airship.

00:21:51.680 --> 00:21:53.880
Will Game...

00:21:53.880 --> 00:21:56.370
So that's where you went.

00:21:56.810 --> 00:21:58.460
Okay, I'm coming.

00:21:58.460 --> 00:22:00.540
You can have it if you like.

00:22:11.490 --> 00:22:15.840
Will... Sir Will Game...

00:22:28.530 --> 00:22:34.540
<b><i>Binetsu ga samenai mama</i></b>

00:22:28.530 --> 00:22:34.540
<b>As if unawoken from a slight fever</b>

00:22:34.540 --> 00:22:40.790
<b><i>Utsumuku shounen no hitomi wa</i></b>

00:22:34.540 --> 00:22:40.790
<b>The eyes of the boy hanging his head</b>

00:22:40.790 --> 00:22:46.510
<b><i>Kokoro no umi mitsumete</i></b>

00:22:40.790 --> 00:22:46.510
<b>Gaze upon the sea of his heart</b>

00:22:46.510 --> 00:22:50.510
<b><i>Shizuka ni hohoenderu</i></b>

00:22:46.510 --> 00:22:50.510
<b>And smile silently</b>

00:22:52.220 --> 00:22:57.020
<b><i>Umare kuru mono kiete yuku mono</i></b>

00:22:52.220 --> 00:22:57.020
<b>What is born, and what fades away</b>

00:22:57.020 --> 00:23:03.230
<b><i>Subete wa sadame no furiko no haba</i></b>

00:22:57.020 --> 00:23:03.230
<b>Are but the sway of the pendulum of fate</b>

00:23:03.230 --> 00:23:08.950
<b><i>Zasetsu no yami o tsukinuke mietekuru</i></b>

00:23:03.230 --> 00:23:08.950
<b>Piercing the darkness of frustration, he begins to see it</b>

00:23:08.950 --> 00:23:14.530
<b><i>Sore ga hikari no shinjitsu</i></b>

00:23:08.950 --> 00:23:14.530
<b>It is the reality of the light</b>

00:23:14.530 --> 00:23:16.870
<b><i>Aura</i></b>

00:23:14.530 --> 00:23:16.870
<b>Aura</b>

00:23:16.870 --> 00:23:25.340
<b><i>Yoake totomoni wasuresareru hoshi ni sasagu</i></b>

00:23:16.870 --> 00:23:25.340
<b>Together with dawn, he gives an offering to the stars that will be forgotten</b>

00:23:25.340 --> 00:23:27.630
<b><i>Aura</i></b>

00:23:25.340 --> 00:23:27.630
<b>Aura</b>

00:23:27.630 --> 00:23:35.510
<b><i>Shijou no ai wa chiisana sono te no naka ni aru</i></b>

00:23:27.630 --> 00:23:35.510
<b>History's love lies in his tiny hands</b>

00:23:40.290 --> 00:23:42.440
<i>Mr. Will Game was seduced by Teteth...</i>

00:23:42.440 --> 00:23:44.650
<i>...and has gone to join Dianna Counter.</i>

00:23:45.150 --> 00:23:48.070
<i>In order to get his wish to go to the moon, he'll do anything.</i>

00:23:48.070 --> 00:23:50.160
<i>Lady Kihel is worried about him.</i>

00:23:51.450 --> 00:23:54.160
<i>I go after him in the White Doll...</i>

00:23:54.160 --> 00:23:56.660
<i>...but become involved in the battle with Lieutenant Harry.</i>

00:23:57.890 --> 00:24:00.650
<i>Next Time... on </i>TURN A GUNDAM...

00:24:00.650 --> 00:24:02.660
Separated Again

00:24:03.420 --> 00:24:04.960
Will the wind disappear?

00:24:03.500 --> 00:24:08.420
<b>Separated Again</b>
